Installed by `sov connect orca` on {{DATE}}.

Write wire: `connectors/harness/orca/mirror.sh` every {{INTERVAL}}s via a scheduled job
(`{{LABEL}}`). It copies `orchestration.db` with its WAL, renders one markdown file per run
into `runs/`, and rewrites a file only when the run changed. `MANIFEST.md` is the heartbeat.

Read wire: none of its own. Orca drives Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and others, and each of
those carries its own Sovereign read wire, so a worker dispatched by Orca already loads
the brain at session start.

What never comes through: Orca's auth and account files, terminal archives, blob storage,
caches, and any field that looks like a credential (withheld at export).
